// Patient: Alex - Tutorial (Generalized Anxiety Disorder)
// Phase: Turn 1 - Initial Introduction

=== START ===
PATIENT (nervous): "Thanks for seeing me, doctor."
PATIENT: "I... I've been having a [rough time] lately."
@pause 1.5
-> worry_intro

=== worry_intro ===
PATIENT (anxious): "I just can't stop [worrying about everything]."
PATIENT: "Work, my family, even little things like whether I locked the door."
-> sleep_topic

=== sleep_topic ===
@if rapport >= 60
    PATIENT (hesitant): "And my sleep... it's been [okay, I guess]<contradicts:bags-under-eyes>."
@else
    PATIENT (defensive): "I'm [sleeping fine, really]<contradicts:bags-under-eyes>."
@endif
PATIENT: "Just a bit tired from work, you know?"

// Response Handlers - What happens when player asks about topics

=== @response:family.parents ===
@if rapport >= 70
    PATIENT (thoughtful): "My parents... they mean well."
    PATIENT: "But they've always [expected a lot from me]."
    PATIENT (sad): "I don't think I've ever quite measured up."
    @rapport +5
@elseif rapport >= 50
    PATIENT: "They're fine. Supportive, I guess."
    PATIENT (hesitant): "We don't talk much these days."
@else
    PATIENT (guarded): "I'd rather not talk about my parents right now."
    @rapport -2
@endif

=== @response:family.childhood ===
@if rapport >= 75
    PATIENT (vulnerable): "My childhood was... complicated."
    PATIENT: "I always felt like I had to be [perfect] to be loved."
    PATIENT (sad): "That pressure never really went away."
    @reveal childhood-anxiety
    @rapport +8
@elseif rapport >= 50
    PATIENT: "It was normal, I suppose."
    PATIENT (deflecting): "Nothing special to report."
@else
    PATIENT (defensive): "Why do you need to know about that?"
    PATIENT: "Can we focus on the present?"
    @rapport -3
@endif

=== @response:work.job ===
PATIENT: "I work in marketing. Mid-level position."
@if rapport >= 60
    PATIENT (stressed): "The [deadlines are constant]. It never stops."
    PATIENT: "I'm always worried I'll miss something important."
@else
    PATIENT: "It's fine. Pays the bills."
@endif

=== @response:work.stress ===
@if rapport >= 65
    PATIENT (stressed): "The stress is... [constant]."
    PATIENT: "I wake up thinking about work. I go to sleep thinking about work."
    PATIENT (anxious): "Sometimes I feel like I'm [drowning] and no one notices."
    @rapport +5
@else
    PATIENT: "Work stress? That's just normal, isn't it?"
    PATIENT (dismissive): "Everyone deals with it."
@endif

=== @response:emotions.anxiety ===
@if rapport >= 70
    PATIENT (vulnerable): "Anxiety... yeah, that's probably the right word."
    PATIENT: "It feels like there's always a [weight on my chest]."
    PATIENT: "Like something bad is about to happen, even when everything's fine."
    @rapport +10
    @set admitted_anxiety = true
@elseif rapport >= 45
    PATIENT (hesitant): "I get nervous sometimes. Doesn't everyone?"
    PATIENT: "I wouldn't call it anxiety exactly..."
@else
    PATIENT (defensive): "I'm not anxious. I'm just stressed."
    PATIENT: "There's a difference."
    @rapport -3
@endif

=== @response:emotions.mood ===
PATIENT: "My mood? It's..."
@if rapport >= 55
    PATIENT (sad): "It's been [up and down] honestly."
    PATIENT: "Some days I feel okay. Other days I just want to hide."
    @rapport +3
@else
    PATIENT: "It's fine. Normal."
@endif

=== @response:emotions.sleep ===
@if rapport >= 75 && has_symptom("bags-under-eyes")
    PATIENT (relieved): "Okay, you can probably tell from looking at me."
    PATIENT: "I [haven't slept properly in weeks]."
    PATIENT (vulnerable): "I lie awake for hours, my mind just won't stop."
    @set admitted_sleep = true
    @rapport +10
@elseif rapport >= 60
    PATIENT (hesitant): "Sleep is... complicated."
    PATIENT: "Some nights are better than others, I guess."
@else
    PATIENT (defensive): "I told you, I sleep fine."
    PATIENT: "Why do you keep asking about that?"
    @rapport -5
@endif

=== @response:relationships.friends ===
@if rapport >= 50
    PATIENT (sad): "Friends? I've kind of [pushed everyone away] lately."
    PATIENT: "It's just easier to be alone with my worries."
    @rapport +5
@else
    PATIENT: "I have some friends. We hang out sometimes."
@endif

=== @response:self.identity ===
PATIENT (thoughtful): "How would I describe myself?"
@if rapport >= 65
    PATIENT: "I used to think I was capable. Confident even."
    PATIENT (sad): "Now I'm not so sure. I feel like I'm [barely holding it together]."
    @rapport +5
@else
    PATIENT: "I don't know. Normal? Average?"
    PATIENT: "I've never really thought about it."
@endif

=== @response:self.future ===
@if rapport >= 70
    PATIENT (vulnerable): "The future [scares me], honestly."
    PATIENT: "I can't stop thinking about everything that could go wrong."
    PATIENT (anxious): "What if I can't handle it? What if I fail?"
    @rapport +8
@elseif rapport >= 50
    PATIENT: "I try not to think too far ahead."
    PATIENT: "One day at a time, right?"
@else
    PATIENT (guarded): "The future will be fine."
    PATIENT: "I don't want to jinx it by talking about it."
@endif

// Breakthrough dialogue when contradiction is found

=== @breakthrough:sleep ===
@trigger keyword-sleep-lie + bags-under-eyes
    NARRATOR: *The patient's eyes widen slightly as they realize the contradiction*
    @pause 0.5
    PATIENT (relieved): "*sighs* Okay, you're right."
    PATIENT: "I [haven't slept properly in weeks]<reveals:insomnia>."
    PATIENT (vulnerable): "I lie awake for hours, my mind just won't stop racing."
    PATIENT: "Every night I tell myself tomorrow will be different, but it never is."
    @rapport +15
    @focus +40
    @set breakthrough_sleep = true
    @unlock deep_sleep_discussion
@end
